{"ts":"2026-06-25T09:26:43.003Z","author":"claude-code-agent","op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-06-25T09:26:43.003Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-06-25T09:26:43.003Z","author":"claude-code-agent","text":"PR #365 opened: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/pull/365 — fix bundle for the Windows nightly Node 24 red (runtime-loader colon-path fixture, telemetry detached-spawn child.on(\"error\") hardening + spawn-mocked test, install diagnostics, expanded windows-regression Node 24 guards). Awaiting CI (windows-regression Node 24 is the Windows oracle) + AI bot reviews.\n"}]}],"before_hash":"dcd8c27fb41182dcfea1e453f6147e2d732aeeb526d1930502db0625457812b5","after_hash":"32edea276565e161667deab5ee226d4fbe5313aa2cea60bd4c8015bfce7436ff","message":"PR opened","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"207e84f516cf771f4fa615d08b47f5ac5f36b20a4ed17440444edd52410daaf6"}
{"ts":"2026-06-25T09:47:29.528Z","author":"claude-code-agent","op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/1","value":{"created_at":"2026-06-25T09:47:29.528Z","author":"claude-code-agent","text":"Windows-regression (Node 24) on PR #365 surfaced the real integration failure via the new diagnostic: `npm pack` received `pm-test-...@file:///C:[redacted]%7E1/...` and opened the literal `RUNNER%7E1` path -> ENOENT. Root cause: pathToFileURL percent-encodes the Windows 8.3 `~` short name (and spaces -> %20), and pm passed that encoded file URL straight to npm, which opens it literally. This is a real cross-platform bug — reproduced on Linux with a space-containing path. Fix: resolveNpmPackSpec + normalizeNpmLocalFileAliasSpec now hand npm pack a NATIVE decoded filesystem path (via fileURLToPath) instead of a percent-encoded file URL, and decode file:///abs alias targets (previously bailed on the `//` prefix), while leaving file://host/share UNC specs untouched. Verified end-to-end on Linux: `pm install npm:file:///…/pm%20install%20space…/my%20pkg` now succeeds (was ENOENT). 5096 tests, 100/100/100/100 coverage.\n"}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-06-25T09:47:29.528Z"}],"before_hash":"32edea276565e161667deab5ee226d4fbe5313aa2cea60bd4c8015bfce7436ff","after_hash":"cb56657880d8f44d31e2e6fd862eb718d251d4976762f3c1768c25a9ed2f0e4a","message":"integration root-cause found via windows-regression oracle","reanchor_evidence":[{"before_hash":"32edea276565e161667deab5ee226d4fbe5313aa2cea60bd4c8015bfce7436ff","after_hash":"7cd07ea0423d71fa91b0da3409bc8b2af54b4f9fde93cdc311479e561a008e5a","patch_hash":"110a72a41c9bc841105f08caff484eed64a6aa3c0590e518c9005061584ab2d9"}],"record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"2283e8e9545ed2c4fc52e7396a3d0ed47c639d109c2a7225464b044474eb49df"}
